                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/1802: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-29T15:00:00+01:00">October 29, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 29—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>582. Referring to the Embassy’s 577 [<hi rendition="#italic">578</hi>], October
                    28, 8 p.m., Geist was officially informed today at German police headquarters
                    that on October 6 the Polish Government issued a decree by virtue of which all
                    passports of Polish Jews abroad became invalid on October 29. German authorities
                    state they are convinced this decree was shortly to be followed by another
                    expatriating all such persons. To prevent these thousands of Polish Jews from
                    becoming stateless and undeportable the German authorities are expelling all
                    Polish male Jews and expect to finish the deportations by tonight. Women and
                    children are not included, it being assumed they will follow voluntarily their
                    male relatives. Police have assured us that they are not deporting Polish Jews
                    holders American immigration visas.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Warsaw and London for Rublee.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
